\"The five cited propositions are all direct packet inputs. The declared application bindings identify the proposed specializations; whether their hypotheses hold is assessed separately under applicability.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First unsupported step is “Smoothness and compact support give continuous compactly supported derivatives”: compact support of u or its derivatives is not an input or consequence of joint smoothness. Subsequent invocation of M001/M003 and the assertion that boundary values of g_j vanish are therefore unsupported. More basically, no decay/integrability condition is supplied to ensure the displayed whole-space integrals exist. The coordinate line integration by parts over [-L,L] does not establish zero boundary values from the stated premises.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/0/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inference/applications/2/hypothesis_checks\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The argument's compact-support, integrability, and vanishing-boundary facts are substantive factual premises not supplied by any listed input or local derivation. Naming M001, M003, and M007 does not prove their hypotheses; M001 only yields integrability after compact support and continuity are established, while the asserted compact support is absent.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/applications/2\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"N003 states the same energy-derivative identity asserted at the end of S001, with the same r>0 scope, integrand, factor 2, and definitions. This judgment concerns statement correspondence only, not derivability.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The inference fixes arbitrary r>0 and purports to establish the corresponding identity; this matches the output's universal r>0 quantification. No temporary assumption is introduced or discharged. The failure is mathematical support, not a quantifier-scope mismatch.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/argument/0\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M001 requires the instantiated integrand to be continuous and compactly supported; continuity may follow from smoothness, but compact support is not given or proved. Consequently M003's product-integrability hypothesis is not established. M007 can provide the interval product-derivative identity only with its stated regularity/integrability hypotheses and yields endpoint values; the proof's further claim that the boundary values vanish is not established. The M010 coordinate-reindexing claim does not supply any of these analytic facts. The specific missing premise is compact support/decay (or another appropriate integrability and boundary argument), not an unchecked source-fidelity issue.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/applications/2\",\"/inference/applications/3\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input and output propositions state their formulas and r>0 quantifier directly; the energy and Laplacian meanings are given by the referenced definitions. The stated formulas can be understood without another inference's proof body.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/definitions/0\",\"/definitions/1\",\"/definitions/2\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The actual prose introduces/uses g_j, the spatial coordinate j, coordinate lines, and L without any local declarations or corresponding statement binders. The packet's locals list declares only r. Even treating these as intended shorthand for standard indices, L is used as a freely chosen endpoint and no scope/introduction basis is recorded. This is an object-closure defect in addition to the substantive missing compact-support fact.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/output/objects\",\"/definitions/0\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Actual factual uses of compact support, whole-space integrability, product integrability, and zero boundary values have no listed input or prior local proof. M001 is conditional and cannot itself supply compact support; the M003 applicability statement relies on the same unsupported premise. Thus the prose's dependency closure fails at its first compact-support assertion.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/0/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inference/applications/1/hypothesis_checks\",\"/inference/argument/0/produces\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Judged from this packet alone: it is insufficient to support R004 because smoothness alone does not provide the compact support, integrability, or vanishing boundary facts used in S001. This is a mathematical review of the supplied packet, not a claim of carrier identity, canonical hash binding, or transmitted-material readback; those are outside this review. No additional source proof or task material was consulted.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/applications/0\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/applications/2\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"premises\":\"The packet gives n,m,u as a jointly smooth map and lists N002 and M001/M003/M007/M010 as inputs; none states compact support or decay of u or its derivatives.\",\"conclusion_used\":\"The derivatives are compactly supported/integrable, and g_j has vanishing boundary values on the coordinate line, so M001/M003 apply and the line integral of ∂_j g_j is zero.\",\"reason\":\"Joint smoothness does not imply compact support, whole-space integrability, or vanishing at infinity. M001 is conditional on compact support, and M007's interval identity retains endpoint terms. No local proof establishes the required facts.\"},{\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"location\":\"/inference/locals\",\"premises\":\"Only r is declared as a local object.\",\"conclusion_used\":\"The proof uses g_j, j, coordinate lines, and L as mathematical objects/indices, including a finite interval [-L,L].\",\"reason\":\"These occurrences have no declaration/introduction and scope in the packet. In particular, no choice or quantification of L is supplied.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"0e7d9ab0-a106-41a1-81cf-6e4ad1376c31","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"e